    <div class="practitioners" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:640px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">
      <div class="practitioner-card reveal">
        <img src="/img/Ssq.jpg" alt="Seb" class="practitioner-photo">
        <div class="practitioner-name">Seb</div>
        <div class="practitioner-role">Qigong &amp; Raja Yoga</div>
        <p class="practitioner-bio">Seb brings over two decades of training in Asian healing arts. He has practised Yoga since 1997, studying with masters in Japan and India, and is a certified Yoga teacher through IYF Asia, qualified in South Korea. Since 2010 he has trained intensively in authentic Qigong, studying and practising with masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland. He is also a certified Therapeutic Thai bodywork therapist and instructor, accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018, with deep additional study in TCM Reflexology. Seb has taught at senior tutor level at the Traditional Thai Massage Association Japan and at the Shivaga Traditional Medical School in Japan, where he delivered Therapeutic Thai Bodywork, Reflexology and Qigong. His deep understanding of Qi cultivation, the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine as they relate to energy work, and hands-on therapeutic bodywork informs every class and session he delivers. Beyond the realm of practice and teaching, Seb is an initiate and direct disciple in the Inchegiri Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>
